o extract EXACT function signatures (parameter names, types, and order).\n\n## Task 2: Update src/actions/output.py\n\n- Add ActionOutput fields based on analysis\n- Implement `print_output()` — check for output utilities in the utility and reuse them here if available\n- Implement `to_dict()` (see `${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/skills/retrieving-context/references/implementation_docs/action_output.md`)\n\n## Task 3: Create Action Files\n\nOne file per action at `actions/<action_name>.py` following the OOP class pattern from `${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/skills/retrieving-context/references/implementation_docs/actions.md`:\n- Each action is a **class** with `__init__(self, input_data: InputFields)` and `execute(self) -> ActionOutput`\n- Initialise the credentials/API client once in `__init__` (see `${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/skills/retrieving-context/references/implementation_docs/credentials.md`)\n- Create OutputFields instance in `__init__`; update it throughout execution\n- Private helpers use `self` — never pass state as explicit arguments\n- Call utilities with EXACT signatures from Task 1 — never guess parameters\n- Use `extension_manager` for error collection and cancellation checks\n- Add logging at method entry, key decision points, and before returns\n\nUpdate the `__init__.py` Output File:\n- Import all action classes\n- Update `ACTION_MAPPER` as lambdas: `\"action_name\": lambda input_data: ClassName(input_data).execute()`\n\n## Task 4: Validate Imports\n\n**Third-party imports** — verify each import path exists in the virtual environment:\n\n```bash\nls ue-dev-env/lib/python*/site-packages/[package_name]/\ngrep -n \"class ClassName\\|def function_name\" ue-dev-env/lib/python*/site-packages/[package_name]/[module].py\n```\n\nNever assume import paths from documentation, verify against the actual installed package.\n\n> **`universal_extension` is exempt from venv verification.** It is a UAC ecosystem module bundled with the Universal Agent — it is never installed in the deve