2026-09-11 08:25:06 - Received stdin data: {"session_id":"1ea84441-e5da-48c6-bba8-6490f5df5280","transcript_path":"/tmp/.claude/projects/-tmp-aws-s3-file-upload/1ea84441-e5da-48c6-bba8-6490f5df5280.jsonl","cwd":"/tmp/aws-s3-file-upload","permission_mode":"bypassPermissions","effort":{"level":"high"},"hook_event_name":"PostToolUse","tool_name":"Read","tool_input":{"file_path":"/tmp/iss-ue-plugin/claude/uac/ue/skills/retrieving-context/references/implementation_docs/actions.md"},"tool_response":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/tmp/iss-ue-plugin/claude/uac/ue/skills/retrieving-context/references/implementation_docs/actions.md","content":"# Actions\n\n## Overview\n\nActions are the business logic implementations mapped to extension operations. Each action is a **class** with an `__init__` that receives `InputFields` and an `execute()` method that returns `ActionOutput`. See `coding-standards.md` for the full OOP rationale.\n\n---\n\n## File: src/actions/__init__.py\n\n```python\nfrom actions.output import ActionOutput\nfrom manager import ExtensionManager\nextension_manager = ExtensionManager()\n\n# Import your action classes\nfrom actions.create_resource import CreateResource\nfrom actions.delete_resource import DeleteResource\n\n# Map action names to lambdas that instantiate the class and call execute()\nACTION_MAPPER = {\n    \"create\": lambda input_data: CreateResource(input_data).execute(),\n    \"delete\": lambda input_data: DeleteResource(input_data).execute(),\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n## Action Class Pattern\n\nEach action is a class. The constructor sets up state; `execute()` orchestrates the operation; private methods handle sub-steps.\n\n```python\nfrom fields import InputFields\nfrom fields.output import OutputFields\nfrom actions.output import ActionOutput\nfrom manager import ExtensionManager\nfrom exceptions import ExecutionError, OperationCancelledError\n\nextension_manager = ExtensionManager()\n\n\nclass CreateResource:\n    def __init__(self, input_data: InputFields) -> None:\n        self._input = input_data\n        self._client = ResourceClient(input_data)   # credentials resolved once; see credentials.md\n        self._output_fields = OutputFields()\n\n    def execute(self) -> ActionOutput:\n        if extension_manager.is_cancelled():\n            raise OperationCancelledError(\"Cancelled before start\")\n\n        result = self._create()\n\n        self._output_fields.update(\n            status=\"Created\",\n            resource_id=result.id,\n        )\n\n        return ActionOutput(\n            resource_id=result.id,\n            resource_name=result.name,\n        )\n\n    def _create(self) -> Resource:\n        return self._client.create(\n            name=self._input.resource_name,\n            region=self._input.region,\n        )\n```\n\n**Why class over function**: Grouping state (input, client, output_fields) as instance attributes removes the need to pass them through every private helper. The `extension_cancel()` hook in `extension.py` can also hold a reference to the action instance and read `action.output_fields.resource_id` without a global singleton.\n\n---\n\n## Accessing UAC Variables\n\nWhen an action needs UAC variables (e.g. task instance ID, workflow variables), read them from `extension_manager.uac_variables`. Do not add UAC variable names as input fields.\n\n```python\nclass CreateResource:\n    def __init__(self, input_data: InputFields) -> None:\n        self._input = input_data\n        self._client = ResourceClient(input_data)\n        uac_vars = extension_manager.uac_variables\n        self._task_instance_id = uac_vars.get(\"taskInstanceId\", \"\")\n\n    def execute(self) -> ActionOutput:\n        unique_name = f\"resource_{self._task_instance_id}\"\n        result = self._client.create(name=unique_name, ...)\n        ...\n```\n\n`uac_variables` always returns a dict — safe to call `.get()` without checking for `None`.\n\n---\n\n## OutputFields Usage (Real-time UI Updates)\n\nUse `OutputFields` for progress tracking and status updates during execution. Each `update()` call syncs automatically to the UAC Controller.\n\n```python\nclass ProcessItems:\n    def __init__(self, input_data: InputFields) -> None:\n        self._input = input_data\n        self._client = ServiceClient(input_data)\n        self._output_fields = OutputFields(\n            status=\"Starting\",\n            progress=\"0%\",\n            items_processed=0,\n        )\n\n    def execute(self) -> ActionOutput:\n        items = self._client.list_items()\n\n        for i, item in enumerate(items):\n            self._output_fields.update(\n                status=\"Processing\",\n                progress=f\"{i + 1}/{len(items)}\",\n                items_processed=i + 1,\n            )\n            self._process_item(item)\n\n        self._output_fields.update(status=\"Completed\", progress=\"100%\")\n\n        return ActionOutput(items_processed=len(items))\n\n    def _process_item(self, item) -> None:\n        ...\n```\n\n**OutputFields sync to the UAC Controller automatically — do not return them from `execute()`.**\n\n---\n\n## Error Handling\n\n**Actions raise errors — `extension.py` catches them.**\n\n### Fail fast (no try-except)\n\n```python\ndef execute(self) -> ActionOutput:\n    # Let utility exceptions propagate — extension.py handles them\n    resource = self._client.find(self._input.resource_id)   # raises ResourceNotFoundError\n    self._client.delete(resource)                            # raises ServiceConnectionError\n    return ActionOutput(resource_id=resource.id)\n```\n\n### Strategic error collection (batch processing only)\n\nUse try-except only when you need to collect errors and continue processing remaining items.\n\n```python\ndef execute(self) -> ActionOutput:\n    processed = 0\n    failed = []\n\n    for item in self._items:\n        try:\n            self._process_item(item)\n            processed += 1\n        except Exception as e:\n            extension_manager.add_error(e, item=item.id)\n            failed.append(item.id)\n\n    if failed:\n        extension_manager.set_result({\"processed\": processed, \"failed\": failed})\n        raise ExecutionError(f\"Failed {len(failed)} of {len(self._items)} items\")\n\n    return ActionOutput(processed=processed)\n```\n\n**Rule: only use try-except in actions for batch error collection. All other errors propagate naturally.**\n\n---\n\n## Path Guards on UAC-Resolved Fields\n\nRequired template fields (file paths, scripts) are resolved and validated by UAC before the extension runs. Do not add `Path(x).exists()` guards on these fields — see `coding-standards.md` §7.\n","numLines":181,"startLine":1,"totalLines":181}},"tool_use_id":"toolu_01756cpYB8ENmsfJPQkP4xjp","duration_ms":1}

